Core API Architecture
🌐 Graph API (Foundation)

Host: graph.facebook.com
Protocol: HTTPS-only, HTTP/1.1
Authentication: OAuth 2.0 access tokens (user, page, app tokens)
Versioning: Quarterly releases (e.g., v25.0, v26.0)
Specify: https://graph.facebook.com/v25.0/...
Default (if omitted): oldest available version ⚠️
Current version: v25.0 (released Feb 18, 2026)
🏗️ Graph Structure

CopyGraph = Nodes + Edges + Fields

Nodes: Individual objects (User, Page, Post, Photo, Video, etc.)
  - Unique ID for each object
  - Example: GET /USER-ID → {name, id}
  - Special endpoint: /me (current token's user/page)

Edges: Connections between nodes
  - Example: GET /USER-ID/photos → list of Photo nodes
  - Returns collections of related objects

Fields: Node properties
  - Default fields returned automatically
  - Custom fields via ?fields=id,name,email,picture
  - Overrides defaults, returns only specified fields + ID
