Pagination Strategies
🎯 Cursor-Based (PREFERRED, most efficient)

Copy{
  "data": [...],
  "paging": {
    "cursors": {
      "after": "MTAxNTExOTQ1MjAwNzI5NDE=",
      "before": "NDMyNzQyODI3OTQw"
    },
    "next": "https://graph.facebook.com/USER-ID/albums?limit=25&after=MTAxNTExOTQ1MjAwNzI5NDE=",
    "previous": "https://graph.facebook.com/USER-ID/albums?limit=25&before=NDMyNzQyODI3OTQw"
  }
}
Parameters: after, before, limit
Stop condition: No next field in response
⚠️ Do NOT store cursors - they invalidate when items deleted
⏰ Time-Based Pagination

CopyGET /USER-ID/feed?since=1364849754&until=1364587774&limit=25
Parameters: since, until (Unix timestamps or strtotime)
Best practice: Specify both for consistent results, max 6-month range
📍 Offset-Based Pagination (last resort)

CopyGET /NODE-ID/edge?offset=50&limit=25
⚠️ Contents shift when new items added
Use only when cursor/time pagination unavailable
